      "username": "The_Justifier",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
      "created_at": "2022-07-02T02:19:11.664Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Wasn’t prepared for how early the second Prison Break happened.  Heroic Interception saved us from a round of damage, but I couldn’t recur it in time.  By the time the Underbosses were all dead, we were on 3 HP each, with the Dragon incoming.  Nightmist hid in Mist Form, and everyone else died; Resurrection Rituals didn’t help, as there was more than 7 damage incoming to anyone after they were raised.  After numerous turns of the careful balancing act required to guard against a Thief, who never appeared, Misty was able to watch safely as Zhu Long obliterated the Operative, then she drew her entire deck and started to drop out of Mist Form, play one Heedless Lash against the Chairman, and go back into Mist Form again on Unity’s turn.  Finally, after a ridiculous length of time, she delivered the deathblow.  Not a very enjoyable fight imo.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
